{
  "dom_id": "step-q120985",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=3{t}^{2}-4t.$ What is the total displacement of the particle between $t=2$ and $t=4?$",
  "worked_solution": "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement. Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}(3{t}^{2}-4t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={({t}^{3}-2{t}^{2})|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =[(4)^{3}-2(4)^{2}]-[(2)^{3}-2(2)^{2}] \\\\  & =[64-32]-[8-8] \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the total displacement between $t=2$ and $t=4$ is $32.$",
